Package: drf
Title: Distributional and Survey-Calibrated Random Forests
Version: 1.4.0
Authors@R: c(
  person(given = "Jeffrey", family = "Naf", email = "jeffrey.naf@unige.ch", role = "cre"),
  person(given = "Loris", family = "Michel", role = "aut"),
  person(given = "Domagoj", family = "Cevid", role = "aut"))
BugReports: https://github.com/lorismichel/drf/issues
Description: Implements distributional random forests as introduced in Cevid, Michel, Naf, Meinshausen, and Buhlmann (2022) <doi:10.48550/arXiv.2005.14458>, together with the root-level primary-sampling-unit-honest Survey-calibrated Distributional Random Forest Algorithm 1 described by Zou, Matabuena, and Kosorok (2026) <doi:10.48550/arXiv.2512.08179>.
License: GPL-3
LinkingTo: Rcpp, RcppEigen
Depends:
    R (>= 3.4.4)
Imports:
    stats,
    fastDummies,
    Matrix,
    methods,
    Rcpp (>= 0.12.15),
    transport
RoxygenNote: 7.3.3
Suggests:
    DiagrammeR,
    testthat (>= 3.0.0),
    torch
Config/testthat/edition: 3
SystemRequirements: GNU make, C++11; CUDA is optional through the suggested torch package
URL: https://github.com/lorismichel/drf
